WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.653
Oxygen and silicon dominate Earth's crust. One silicon surrounded by four

00:00:04.653 --> 00:00:08.955
oxygens makes a tetrahedron, the basic silicate unit. Learn both the

00:00:08.955 --> 00:00:10.520
structure and its name.

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:16.368
Sharing corner oxygens links tetrahedra into chains, sheets, and frameworks. He

00:00:16.368 --> 00:00:21.385
also asked about non-silicates: name their group from the anion. Sulfide

00:00:21.385 --> 00:00:26.403
and sulfate differ because sulfate contains oxygen. Review ionic, covalent, metallic,

00:00:26.403 --> 00:00:29.140
and molecular bonds alongside these structures.
